---@class okta.AuthenticatorKeyTacInputProvider
---@field type? okta.AuthenticatorKeyTacInputProviderType|string Provider type
---@field configuration? okta.AuthenticatorKeyTacInputProviderConfiguration Define the configuration settings of the TAC

---Define the configuration settings of the TAC
---@class okta.AuthenticatorKeyTacInputProviderConfiguration
---@field minTtl number Minimum time-to-live (TTL) of the TAC in minutes. The `minTtl` indicates the minimum amount of time that a TAC is valid. The `minTtl` must be less than the `maxTtl`.
---@field maxTtl number Maximum TTL of the TAC in minutes. The `maxTtl` indicates the maximum amount of time that a TAC is valid. The `maxTtl` must be greater than the `minTtl`.
---@field defaultTtl number The default TTL in minutes when you create a TAC. The `defaultTtl` indicates the actual amount of time that a TAC is valid before it expires. The `defaultTtl` must be greater than the `minTtl` and less than the `maxTtl`.
---@field length number Defines the number of characters in a TAC. For example, a `length` of `16` means that the TAC is 16 characters.
---@field complexity okta.AuthenticatorKeyTacInputProviderConfigurationComplexity Define the complexity of the TAC
---@field multiUseAllowed? boolean Indicates whether a TAC can be used multiple times. If set to `true`, the TAC can be used multiple times until it expires.

---Define the complexity of the TAC
---@class okta.AuthenticatorKeyTacInputProviderConfigurationComplexity
---@field numbers? boolean Use numbers in the TAC. `numbers` is always `true` for the TAC authenticator.
---@field letters? boolean Use letters in the TAC
---@field specialCharacters? boolean Use special characters in the TAC

