---@field enabled? boolean Indicates whether the provider is enabled and can be used
---@field id? string ID of the custom telephony provider
---@field isPrimaryProvider? boolean Indicates whether the provider is the primary telephony provider
---@field providerCapability? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderCredentialResponseProviderCapability The types of telephony operations (SMS or Voice) that you use with your telephony provider. `ALL` is the only valid value. It indicates that your provider can handle both SMS messages and voice calls. You're not required to use both types of telephony operations, but your provider can support both.
---@field providerName? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderCredentialResponseProviderName Name of the telephony provider
---@field providerSettings? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettings
---@field providerSid? string The account string identifier (SID) for your telephony provider account. Your telephony provider gives you this SID.

---The types of telephony operations (SMS or Voice) that you use with your telephony provider.
---
---`ALL` is the only valid value. It indicates that your provider can handle both SMS messages and voice calls. You're not required to use both types of telephony operations, but your provider can support both.
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderCredentialResponseProviderCapability "ALL"

---Name of the telephony provider
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderCredentialResponseProviderName "TWILIO"|"TELESIGN"

---Response for credentials of multiple custom telephony providers
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderCredentialsResponse okta.CustomTelephonyProviderCredentialResponse[]

---Settings for custom telephony provider.
---
---These settings vary based on the telephony provider and the type of telephony operation (SMS or Voice). For `sms` and `call`, you can select one method per telephony operation (`sms` and `call`) for sending messages or voice calls.
---
---> **Note:** Configure your telephony provider settings before selecting the methods for sending SMS messages or making voice calls. For example, if you select Twilio as your telephony provider, and you want to send SMS messages using Twilio's Verify Service, ensure that you have the Verify Service set up in your Twilio account. You can then use the `twilioVerifySid` field under `sms` to provide the necessary SID.
---@class okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettings
---@field call? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsCall Method for making voice calls. Choose one method for making voice calls based on your telephony provider setup.
---@field sms? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsSms Method for sending SMS messages. Choose one method for sending SMS messages based on your telephony provider setup.

---Method for making voice calls. Choose one method for making voice calls based on your telephony provider setup.
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsCall okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTwilioVerify|okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTwilioPhoneNumber|okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTwilioCallerId|okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceCall

---Method for sending SMS messages. Choose one method for sending SMS messages based on your telephony provider setup.
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsSms okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTwilioVerify|okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTwilioPhoneNumber|okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTwilioMessagingService|okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceSms

---@class okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceCall
---@field telesignService? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceCallTelesignService|string The Telesign service identifier used for sending making calls. You can find this value in your Telesign console. The `telesignVerifyService` method uses Telesign's [Verify API](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/verify-api-overview). And the `telesignVoiceService` method uses Telesign's [Voice API](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/voice-overview).

---The Telesign service identifier used for sending making calls. You can find this value in your Telesign console.
---
---The `telesignVerifyService` method uses Telesign's [Verify API](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/verify-api-overview). And the `telesignVoiceService` method uses Telesign's [Voice API](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/voice-overview).
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceCallTelesignService "telesignVoiceService"|"telesignVerifyService"

---@class okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceSms
---@field telesignService? okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceSmsTelesignService|string The Telesign service identifier used for sending SMS messages. You can find this value in your Telesign console. The `telesignVerifyService` method uses Telesign's [Verify API](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/verify-api-overview). And the `telesignMessagingService` method uses Telesign's [SMS](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/voice-overview) and [Messaging](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/messaging-overview) APIs.

---The Telesign service identifier used for sending SMS messages. You can find this value in your Telesign console.
---
---The `telesignVerifyService` method uses Telesign's [Verify API](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/verify-api-overview). And the `telesignMessagingService` method uses Telesign's [SMS](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/voice-overview) and [Messaging](https://developer.telesign.com/enterprise/docs/messaging-overview) APIs.
---@alias okta.CustomTelephonyProviderSettingsTelesignServiceSmsTelesignService "telesignMessagingService"|"telesignVerifyService"

