---@class okta.ListApplicationsRequest
---@field q? string Searches for apps with `name` or `label` properties that starts with the `q` value using the `startsWith` operation
---@field after? string Specifies the [pagination](/#pagination) cursor for the next page of results. Treat this as an opaque value obtained through the `next` link relationship.
---@field useOptimization? boolean Specifies whether to use query optimization. If you specify `useOptimization=true` in the request query, the response contains a subset of app instance properties.
---@field alwaysIncludeVpnSettings? boolean Specifies whether to include the VPN configuration for existing notifications in the result, regardless of whether VPN notifications are configured
---@field limit? number Specifies the number of results per page
---@field filter? string Filters apps with a supported expression for a subset of properties. Filtering supports the following limited number of properties: `id`, `status`, `credentials.signing.kid`, `settings.slo.enabled`, or `name`. See [Filter](https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/#filter).
---@field expand? string An optional parameter used for link expansion to embed more resources in the response. Only supports `expand=user/{userId}` and must be used with the `user.id eq "{userId}"` filter query for the same user. Returns the assigned [application user](/openapi/okta-management/management/tags/applicationusers) in the `_embedded` property.
---@field includeNonDeleted? boolean Specifies whether to include non-active, but not deleted apps in the results

