---@class okta.OAuth2Claim
---@field alwaysIncludeInToken? boolean Specifies whether to include Claims in the token. The value is always `TRUE` for access token Claims. If the value is set to `FALSE` for an ID token claim, the Claim isn't included in the ID token when the token is requested with the access token or with the `authorization_code`. The client instead uses the access token to get Claims from the `/userinfo` endpoint.
---@field claimType? okta.OAuth2ClaimType
---@field conditions? okta.OAuth2ClaimConditions
---@field group_filter_type? okta.OAuth2ClaimGroupFilterType
---@field id? string ID of the Claim
---@field name? string Name of the Claim
---@field status? okta.LifecycleStatus
---@field system? boolean When `true`, indicates that Okta created the Claim
---@field value? string Specifies the value of the Claim. This value must be a string literal if `valueType` is `GROUPS`, and the string literal is matched with the selected `group_filter_type`. The value must be an Okta EL expression if `valueType` is `EXPRESSION`.
---@field valueType? okta.OAuth2ClaimValueType
---@field _links? okta.LinksSelf

---Specifies the scopes for the Claim
---@class okta.OAuth2ClaimConditions
---@field scopes? okta.OAuth2ClaimConditionsScopesList

---@alias okta.OAuth2ClaimConditionsScopesList string[]

---Specifies the type of group filter if `valueType` is `GROUPS`
---
---If `valueType` is `GROUPS`, then the groups returned are filtered according to the value of `group_filter_type`.
---
---If you have complex filters for Groups, you can [create a Groups allowlist](https://developer.okta.com/docs/guides/customize-tokens-groups-claim/main/) to put them all in a Claim.
---@alias okta.OAuth2ClaimGroupFilterType "CONTAINS"|"EQUALS"|"REGEX"|"STARTS_WITH"

---Specifies whether the Claim is for an access token (`RESOURCE`) or an ID token (`IDENTITY`)
---@alias okta.OAuth2ClaimType "IDENTITY"|"RESOURCE"

---Specifies whether the Claim is an Okta Expression Language (EL) expression (`EXPRESSION`), a set of groups (`GROUPS`), or a system claim (`SYSTEM`)
---@alias okta.OAuth2ClaimValueType "EXPRESSION"|"GROUPS"|"SYSTEM"

