---Specifies the OS requirement for the policy.
---
---There are two types of OS requirements:
---
---* **Static**: A specific OS version requirement that doesn't change until you update the policy. A static OS requirement is specified with the `osVersion.minimum` property.
---* **Dynamic**: An OS version requirement that is relative to the latest major OS release and security patch. A dynamic OS requirement is specified with the `osVersion.dynamicVersionRequirement` property.
---> **Note:** Dynamic OS requirements are available only if the **Dynamic OS version compliance** [self-service EA](/openapi/okta-management/guides/release-lifecycle/#early-access-ea) feature is enabled. You can't specify both `osVersion.minimum` and `osVersion.dynamicVersionRequirement` properties at the same time.
---@class okta.OSVersion
---@field dynamicVersionRequirement? okta.OSVersionDynamicVersionRequirement Contains the necessary properties for a dynamic version requirement
---@field minimum? string The device version must be equal to or newer than the specified version string (maximum of three components for iOS and macOS, and maximum of four components for Android)

---@class okta.OSVersionConstraint
---@field dynamicVersionRequirement? okta.OSVersionConstraintDynamicVersionRequirement Contains the necessary properties for a dynamic Windows version requirement
---@field majorVersionConstraint okta.OSVersionConstraintMajorVersionConstraint|string Indicates the Windows major version
---@field minimum? string The Windows device version must be equal to or newer than the specified version

---Contains the necessary properties for a dynamic Windows version requirement
---@class okta.OSVersionConstraintDynamicVersionRequirement
---@field type? okta.OSVersionConstraintDynamicVersionRequirementType|string Indicates the type of the dynamic Windows version requirement
---@field distanceFromLatestMajor? number Indicates the distance from the latest Windows major version
---@field latestSecurityPatch? boolean Indicates whether the policy requires Windows devices to be on the latest security patch

---Indicates the type of the dynamic Windows version requirement
---@alias okta.OSVersionConstraintDynamicVersionRequirementType "MINIMUM"|"EXACT"|"EXACT_ANY_SUPPORTED"|"NOT_ALLOWED"

---Indicates the Windows major version
---@alias okta.OSVersionConstraintMajorVersionConstraint "WINDOWS_11"|"WINDOWS_10"

---Contains the necessary properties for a dynamic version requirement
---@class okta.OSVersionDynamicVersionRequirement
---@field type? okta.OSVersionDynamicVersionRequirementType|string Indicates the type of the dynamic OS version requirement
---@field distanceFromLatestMajor? number Indicates the distance from the latest major version
---@field latestSecurityPatch? boolean Indicates whether the device needs to be on the latest security patch

---Indicates the type of the dynamic OS version requirement
---@alias okta.OSVersionDynamicVersionRequirementType "MINIMUM"|"EXACT"|"EXACT_ANY_SUPPORTED"

---Current version of the operating system (maximum of four components in the versioning scheme)
