---Properties governing the user's session lifetime
---@class okta.OktaSignOnPolicyRuleSignonSessionActions
---@field maxSessionIdleMinutes? number Maximum number of minutes that a user session can be idle before the session is ended
---@field maxSessionLifetimeMinutes? number Maximum number of minutes (from when the user signs in) that a user's session is active. Set this to force users to sign in again after the number of specified minutes. Disable by setting to `0`.
---@field usePersistentCookie? boolean If set to `false`, user session cookies only last the length of a browser session. If set to `true`, user session cookies last across browser sessions. This setting doesn't impact administrators who can never have persistent session cookies. This property is read-only for the default rule of the default global session policy.

