---@class okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettings
---@field emOptInStatus? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsEmOptInStatus The entitlement management opt-in status for the app
---@field identityStoreId? string Identifies an additional identity store app, if your app supports it. The `identityStoreId` value must be a valid identity store app ID. This identity store app must be created in the same org as your app.
---@field implicitAssignment? boolean Controls whether Okta automatically assigns users to the app based on the user's role or group membership.
---@field inlineHookId? string Identifier of an inline hook. Inline hooks are outbound calls from Okta to your own custom code, triggered at specific points in Okta process flows. They allow you to integrate custom functionality into those flows. See [Inline hooks](/openapi/okta-management/management/tags/inlinehook/).
---@field notes? okta.ApplicationSettingsNotes
---@field notifications? okta.ApplicationSettingsNotifications
---@field oauthClient? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClient

---@class okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClient
---@field application_type? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationType
---@field backchannel_authentication_request_signing_alg? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientBackchannelAuthenticationRequestSigningAlg The signing algorithm for Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA) signed requests using JWT. If this value isn't set and a JWT-signed request is sent, the request fails. > **Note:** This property appears for clients with `urn:openid:params:grant-type:ciba` defined as one of the `grant_types`.
---@field backchannel_custom_authenticator_id? string The ID of the custom authenticator that authenticates the user > **Note:** This property appears for clients with `urn:openid:params:grant-type:ciba` defined as one of the `grant_types`.
---@field backchannel_token_delivery_mode? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientBackchannelTokenDeliveryMode The delivery mode for Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA). Currently, only `poll` is supported. > **Note:** This property appears for clients with `urn:openid:params:grant-type:ciba` defined as one of the `grant_types`.
---@field client_uri? string URL string of a web page providing information about the client
---@field consent_method? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationConsentMethod
---@field dpop_bound_access_tokens? boolean Indicates that the client application uses Demonstrating Proof-of-Possession (DPoP) for token requests. If `true`, the authorization server rejects token requests from this client that don't contain the DPoP header. > **Note:** If `dpop_bound_access_tokens` is true, then `client_credentials` and `implicit` aren't allowed in `grant_types`.
---@field frontchannel_logout_session_required? boolean <x-lifecycle-container><x-lifecycle class="ea"></x-lifecycle> <x-lifecycle class="oie"></x-lifecycle></x-lifecycle-container>Determines whether Okta sends `sid` and `iss` in the logout request
---@field frontchannel_logout_uri? string <x-lifecycle-container><x-lifecycle class="ea"></x-lifecycle> <x-lifecycle class="oie"></x-lifecycle></x-lifecycle-container>URL where Okta sends the logout request
---@field grant_types okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientGrantTypesList
---@field id_token_encrypted_response_alg? okta.IdTokenKeyEncryptionAlgorithm
---@field idp_initiated_login? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationIdpInitiatedLogin
---@field initiate_login_uri? string URL string that a third party can use to initiate the sign-in flow by the client
---@field issuer_mode? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationIssuerMode
---@field jwks? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientKeys
---@field jwks_uri? string URL string that references a JSON Web Key Set for validating JWTs presented to Okta or for encrypting ID tokens minted by Okta for the client
---@field logo_uri? string The URL string that references a logo for the client. This logo appears on the client tile in the End-User Dashboard. It also appears on the client consent dialog during the client consent flow.
---@field network? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationNetwork
---@field participate_slo? boolean <x-lifecycle-container><x-lifecycle class="ea"></x-lifecycle> <x-lifecycle class="oie"></x-lifecycle></x-lifecycle-container>Allows the app to participate in front-channel Single Logout > **Note:** You can only enable `participate_slo` for `web` and `browser` application types (`application_type`).
---@field policy_uri? string URL string of a web page providing the client's policy document
---@field post_logout_redirect_uris? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientPostLogoutRedirectUrisList Array of redirection URI strings for relying party-initiated logouts
---@field redirect_uris? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientRedirectUrisList Array of redirection URI strings for use in redirect-based flows. > **Note:** At least one `redirect_uris` and `response_types` are required for all client types, with exceptions: if the client uses the [Resource Owner Password ](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6749#section-4.3)flow (`grant_types` contains `password`) or [Client Credentials](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6749#section-4.4)flow (`grant_types` contains `client_credentials`), then no `redirect_uris` or `response_types` is necessary. In these cases, you can pass either null or an empty array for these attributes.
---@field refresh_token? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsRefreshToken
---@field request_object_signing_alg? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientRequestObjectSigningAlg The type of JSON Web Key Set (JWKS) algorithm that must be used for signing request objects
---@field response_types? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientResponseTypesList Array of OAuth 2.0 response type strings
---@field sector_identifier_uri? string The sector identifier used for pairwise `subject_type`. See [OIDC Pairwise Identifier Algorithm](https://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-messages-1_0-20.html#idtype.pairwise.alg)
---@field subject_type? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientSubjectType Type of the subject
---@field tos_uri? string URL string of a web page providing the client's terms of service document
---@field wildcard_redirect? okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientWildcardRedirect Indicates if the client is allowed to use wildcard matching of `redirect_uris`

---The signing algorithm for Client-Initiated Backchannel Authentication (CIBA) signed requests using JWT. If this value isn't set and a JWT-signed request is sent, the request fails.
---> **Note:** This property appears for clients with `urn:openid:params:grant-type:ciba` defined as one of the `grant_types`.
---@alias okta.OpenIdConnectApplicationSettingsClientBackchannelAuthenticationRequestSigningAlg "HS256"|"HS384"|"HS512"|"RS256"|"RS384"|"RS512"|"ES256"|"ES384"|"ES512"

