---Age settings
---@class okta.PasswordPolicyPasswordSettingsAge
---@field expireWarnDays? number Specifies the number of days prior to password expiration when a User is warned to reset their password: `0` indicates no warning
---@field historyCount? number Specifies the number of distinct passwords that a User must create before they can reuse a previous password: `0` indicates none
---@field maxAgeDays? number Specifies how long (in days) a password remains valid before it expires: `0` indicates no limit
---@field minAgeMinutes? number Specifies the minimum time interval (in minutes) between password changes: `0` indicates no limit

---Breached Protection settings
---@class okta.PasswordPolicyPasswordSettingsBreachedProtection
---@field delegatedWorkflowId? string|distilled.Null The `id` of the workflow that runs when a breached password is found during a sign-in attempt.
---@field expireAfterDays? number|distilled.Null Specifies the number of days after a breached password is found during a sign-in attempt that the user's password should expire. Valid values: 0 through 10. If set to 0, it happens immediately.
---@field logoutEnabled? boolean|distilled.Null (Optional, default is false) If true, you must also specify a value for `expireAfterDays`. When enabled, the user's session(s) are terminated immediately the first time the user's credentials are detected as part of a breach.

---Complexity settings
---@class okta.PasswordPolicyPasswordSettingsComplexity
---@field dictionary? okta.PasswordDictionary
---@field excludeAttributes? okta.PasswordPolicyPasswordSettingsComplexityExcludeAttributesList The User profile attributes whose values must be excluded from the password: currently only supports `firstName` and `lastName`
---@field excludeUsername? boolean Indicates if the Username must be excluded from the password
---@field maxConsecutiveCharacters? number <x-lifecycle-container><x-lifecycle class="oie"></x-lifecycle></x-lifecycle-container>Specifies the maximum number of consecutive repeating characters that can be used in a password
---@field minLength? number Minimum password length
---@field minLowerCase? number Indicates if a password must contain at least one lower case letter: `0` indicates no, `1` indicates yes
---@field minNumber? number Indicates if a password must contain at least one number: `0` indicates no, `1` indicates yes
---@field minSymbol? number Indicates if a password must contain at least one symbol (For example: !@#$%^&*): `0` indicates no, `1` indicates yes
---@field minUpperCase? number Indicates if a password must contain at least one upper case letter: `0` indicates no, `1` indicates yes
---@field oelStatement? string <x-lifecycle-container><x-lifecycle class="oie"></x-lifecycle></x-lifecycle-container>Use an [Expression Language](https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/okta-expression-language-in-identity-engine/) expression to block a word from being used in a password. You can only block one word per expression. Use the `OR` operator to connect multiple expressions to block multiple words.

---The User profile attributes whose values must be excluded from the password: currently only supports `firstName` and `lastName`
---@alias okta.PasswordPolicyPasswordSettingsComplexityExcludeAttributesList string[]

