---@field destination? string Identifies the location inside the SAML assertion where the SAML response should be sent
---@field destinationOverride? string Destination override for CASB configuration. See [CASB config guide](https://help.okta.com/en-us/Content/Topics/Apps/CASB-config-guide.htm).
---@field digestAlgorithm? okta.SamlApplicationSettingsSignOnDigestAlgorithm|string Determines the digest algorithm used to digitally sign the SAML assertion and response
---@field honorForceAuthn boolean Set to `true` to prompt users for their credentials when a SAML request has the `ForceAuthn` attribute set to `true`
---@field idpIssuer? string SAML Issuer ID
---@field inlineHooks? okta.SamlApplicationSettingsSignOnInlineHooksList Associates the app with SAML inline hooks. See [the SAML assertion inline hook reference](https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/saml-hook/).
---@field participateSlo? okta.SloParticipate
---@field recipient? string The location where the app may present the SAML assertion
---@field recipientOverride? string Recipient override for CASB configuration. See [CASB config guide](https://help.okta.com/en-us/Content/Topics/Apps/CASB-config-guide.htm).
---@field requestCompressed boolean Determines whether the SAML request is expected to be compressed
---@field responseSigned boolean Determines whether the SAML authentication response message is digitally signed by the IdP > **Note:** Either (or both) `responseSigned` or `assertionSigned` must be `TRUE`.
---@field samlAssertionLifetimeSeconds? number Determines the SAML app session lifetimes with Okta
---@field signatureAlgorithm? okta.SamlApplicationSettingsSignOnSignatureAlgorithm|string Determines the signing algorithm used to digitally sign the SAML assertion and response
---@field slo? okta.SingleLogout
---@field spCertificate? okta.SamlSpCertificate
