---@field oneOf? okta.UserSchemaAttributeOneOfList|distilled.Null Non-empty array of valid JSON schemas. The `oneOf` key is only supported in conjunction with `enum` and provides a mechanism to return a display name for the `enum` value.<br> Each schema has the following format: ``` { "const": "enumValue", "title": "display name" } ``` When `enum` is used in conjunction with `oneOf`, you must keep the set of enumerated values and their order.<br> For example: ``` "enum": ["S","M","L","XL"], "oneOf": [ {"const": "S", "title": "Small"}, {"const": "M", "title": "Medium"}, {"const": "L", "title": "Large"}, {"const": "XL", "title": "Extra Large"} ] ```
